    <h1>About This Directory</h1>

    <p>
      When you need care for a parent or loved one, the last thing you want is to scroll through a national website that doesn't know Schuylkill County from Schenectady. We built this directory because Coal Region families deserve a local resource — built by locals, for locals — to find trusted care providers without the guesswork.
    </p>

    <h2>Why We Built This</h2>
    <p>
      Searching for senior care is overwhelming. You're dealing with unfamiliar terminology, emotional weight, and time pressure — all while trying to make the best decision for someone you love. National directories bury rural Pennsylvania under a mountain of sponsored results and out-of-area providers.
    </p>
    <p>
      This directory exists so that when a Coal Region family needs to find assisted living, home health, hospice, or a nursing home, they have one clear, local place to look. No sales pitches. No sponsored rankings. Just real providers serving real families in our community.
    </p>

    <h2>What We Include</h2>
    <p>
      Every listing includes publicly available information: name, address, phone number, website, and Google ratings where available. We don't accept payment for placement or rankings — listings are organized alphabetically by city.
    </p>

    <h2>This Is a Community Resource</h2>
    <p>
      This directory is not a sales platform. We don't steer families toward one provider over another. We don't take referral fees. We simply want to make it easier for families to find the care their loved ones need, in the community where they've lived their whole lives.
    </p>

    <h2>About Antigravity</h2>
    <p>
      This directory is maintained by <strong>Antigravity Digital Services</strong>, a digital services company helping local businesses in the Coal Region strengthen their online presence. We believe that the providers who care for our community's elders deserve modern tools to reach the families who need them.
    </p>

    <p>
      <a href="/contact/">Have a question or correction? Contact us.</a>
    </p>
